# Explain with comments

Every function, constant, and variable gets a comment that says what it is for. Write the comment for a reader who has not seen the code. Explain the role. Do not restate the name.

Use a JSDoc block on functions and on exported constants. Name each parameter and the return value. Use one line comment above a local variable or a private constant.

```tsx
/** Dayjs format token for a calendar date: `YYYY-MM-DD`. */
export const ISO_DATE = 'YYYY-MM-DD'

/**
 * Builds the next range after the user picks `day`.
 * An empty range starts at `day`. A range with only a start becomes a pair,
 * ordered so the earlier day is first.
 * @param current - The range before this pick. Either element may be null.
 * @param day - The picked day, as `YYYY-MM-DD`.
 * @returns The range to store after the pick.
 */
function nextRange(current: DateRangeValue, day: string): DateRangeValue {
  // True when this cell is the first day of the highlighted range.
  const isFrom = range.from?.isSame(day, 'day') ?? false
}
```
